06649952,-0.04174815,-0.01824742,0.09064719,-0.00501611,0.04908269,-0.11085007,0.00482032,0.00545671,0.14514649,-0.05545176,0.00472467,0.0707675,0.00591776,-0.0231251,0.00016569,-0.0174417,0.03858291,0.00871844,0.11206537,0.01561477,0.05576213,0.08980403,-0.03336963,-0.04495678,0.02256434,-0.01743972,0.07662984,0.02326359,-0.01117836,-0.01984923,0.09308784,-0.01340496,0.03773459,-0.03105979,0.01281415,0.02552208,0.02840114,0.00459034,-0.02952759,0.00182428,0.05801409,-0.00630958,0.00590115,-0.0134212,-0.02505612,-0.0591468,0.03395859,-0.04379563,-0.0049017,0.05992915,-0.04164565],"last_embed":{"hash":"1r6lx8f","tokens":453}}},"last_read":{"hash":"1r6lx8f","at":1778067910484},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1774939523000,"size":4820,"at":1778067900854,"hash":"1r6lx8f"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,18],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model":[20,42],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#{1}":[21,25],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#📝 Benim Notlarım":[26,28],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[29,31],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[32,34],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[33,34],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[35,37],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42],"#Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)#{1}":[42,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/89LNGS2Y","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XELACWFK?page=1&annotation=IN8NYJ3M","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XELACWFK?page=1&annotation=Y848FP3X","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XELACWFK?page=1&annotation=HW96XVTJ","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 9","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XELACWFK?page=9&annotation=G9YP5C5E","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 10","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/XELACWFK?page=10&annotation=YPAK3J8F","line":42}],"metadata":{"Title":"Artificial Intelligence-Based Hospital Malnutrition Screening: Validation of a Novel Machine Learning Model","Authors":"Adam M. Bernstein, Pierre Janeke, Richard V. Riggs, Emily Burke, Jemima Meyer, Meagan F. Moyer, Keiy Murofushi, Raymond A. Botha, Josiah El Michael Meyer","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.1055/a-2635-3158","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"The objectives of the study were to evaluate an AI-based hospital malnutrition screening model in a large and diverse inpatient population and to compare it to the currently used clinician-delivered malnutrition screening tool.We studied the performance of a gradient-boosted decision tree model incorporating a large language model (LLM) for feature extraction using the electronic medical record data of 106,449 patients over 3.75 years.","Findings":"The model’s area under the receiver operating curve was 0.92 (95% confidence interval [CI]: 0.91–0.92) on the first day of hospitalization and rose to 0.95 (95% CI: 0.95–0.96) using the maximum risk predicted for each patient throughout hospitalization, indexed against discharge-coded malnutrition. Similar results were observed when indexed against dietitian-recorded malnutrition. The model outperformed the nurse-administered, modified version of the Malnutrition Screening Tool (MST) that was used in practice. Patients identified by the model had higher likelihoods of readmission and death compared with patients identified by the nurse-administered screener.In this large retrospective analysis, we found that a novel AI model identified patients at risk of malnutrition with a high degree of sensitivity and specificity overall when indexed against either dietitian-recorded malnutrition or discharge-coded malnutrition. T","Conclusions":"","Limitations":"single hospital using inpatient data. Yet with the breadth of demographic and health characteristics of patients admitted, the results likely have strong external generalizability.  Importantly, too, the features selected by the model are widely available at other hospitals. T","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1r6lx8f","at":1774939762917},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/bernsteinArtificialIntelligenceBasedHospital2025a.md"},
